        "text": "In the old days I remember a wind that would blow down through the canyons before dawn. It was a hot wind and carried with it the smell of warm places. It blew strongest before dawn across The Point. ly friends and I would Sleep in our cars -- ,"
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 7,
        "line": 835,
        "text": "Bear had said it. ‘a day will come that is like no other -- a dav that is so hig -- so grand an event of nature that it cleans everything that went before it. and nothing that happens after it will ever be the same.'"
      }
